WEBVTT

00:08:29.621 --> 00:08:32.579
when I met Mohamed
outside a post office at noon.

00:08:33.246 --> 00:08:34.746
He listened to me.

00:08:35.496 --> 00:08:38.329
You know, it was most often
when speaking to people

00:08:38.371 --> 00:08:41.496
that I wondered where I ended
and my disability began.

00:08:42.329 --> 00:08:45.204
For many people told me
what they told no one else.

00:08:45.246 --> 00:08:46.621
Many cried.

00:08:47.287 --> 00:08:50.079
And one day, after a woman
I met on the street did the same

00:08:50.079 --> 00:08:51.912
and I later asked her why,

00:08:51.954 --> 00:08:53.787
she told me that, best she could tell,

00:08:53.829 --> 00:08:57.287
her tears had had something to do
with my being happy and strong,

00:08:57.329 --> 00:08:58.871
but vulnerable too.

00:08:59.787 --> 00:09:02.204
I listened to her words,
I suppose they were true.